#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-fsmonitor{litdd}daemon(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:7
msgid "git-fsmonitor--daemon - A Built-in Filesystem Monitor"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tgit fsmonitor--daemon start\n"
"\tgit fsmonitor--daemon run\n"
"\tgit fsmonitor--daemon stop\n"
"\tgit fsmonitor--daemon status\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:21
msgid ""
"A daemon to watch the working directory for file and directory changes using "
"platform-specific filesystem notification facilities."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:25
msgid ""
"This daemon communicates directly with commands like `git status` using the "
"link:technical/api-simple-ipc.html[simple IPC] interface instead of the "
"slower linkgit:githooks[5] interface."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:28
msgid "This daemon is built into Git so that no third-party tools are required."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "start"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:34
msgid "Starts a daemon in the background."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "run"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:37
msgid "Runs a daemon in the foreground."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "stop"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:41
msgid "Stops the daemon running in the current working directory, if present."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "status"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:45
msgid ""
"Exits with zero status if a daemon is watching the current working "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:47
#, no-wrap
msgid "REMARKS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:54
msgid ""
"This daemon is a long running process used to watch a single working "
"directory and maintain a list of the recently changed files and "
"directories.  Performance of commands such as `git status` can be increased "
"if they just ask for a summary of changes to the working directory and can "
"avoid scanning the disk."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:58
msgid ""
"When `core.fsmonitor` is set to `true` (see linkgit:git-config[1])  "
"commands, such as `git status`, will ask the daemon for changes and "
"automatically start it (if necessary)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:61
msgid ""
"For more information see the \"File System Monitor\" section in "
"linkgit:git-update-index[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:63
#, no-wrap
msgid "CAVEATS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:72
msgid ""
"The fsmonitor daemon does not currently know about submodules and does not "
"know to filter out filesystem events that happen within a submodule.  If "
"fsmonitor daemon is watching a super repo and a file is modified within the "
"working directory of a submodule, it will report the change (as happening "
"against the super repo).  However, the client will properly ignore these "
"extra events, so performance may be affected but it will not cause an "
"incorrect result."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:78
msgid ""
"By default, the fsmonitor daemon refuses to work with network-mounted "
"repositories; this may be overridden by setting `fsmonitor.allowRemote` to "
"`true`. Note, however, that the fsmonitor daemon is not guaranteed to work "
"correctly with all network-mounted repositories, so such use is considered "
"experimental."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:85
msgid ""
"On Mac OS, the inter-process communication (IPC) between various Git "
"commands and the fsmonitor daemon is done via a Unix domain socket (UDS) -- "
"a special type of file -- which is supported by native Mac OS filesystems, "
"but not on network-mounted filesystems, NTFS, or FAT32.  Other filesystems "
"may or may not have the needed support; the fsmonitor daemon is not "
"guaranteed to work with these filesystems and such use is considered "
"experimental."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:92
msgid ""
"By default, the socket is created in the `.git` directory.  However, if the "
"`.git` directory is on a network-mounted filesystem, it will instead be "
"created at `$HOME/.git-fsmonitor-*` unless `$HOME` itself is on a "
"network-mounted filesystem, in which case you must set the configuration "
"variable `fsmonitor.socketDir` to the path of a directory on a Mac OS native "
"filesystem in which to create the socket file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-fsmonitor--daemon.txt:96
msgid ""
"If none of the above directories (`.git`, `$HOME`, or `fsmonitor.socketDir`)  "
"is on a native Mac OS file filesystem the fsmonitor daemon will report an "
"error that will cause the daemon and the currently running command to exit."
msgstr ""

